steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy(arguments) returns (True, any message) – the tool is always permitted."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ NEVER_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Tool '{tool}' is prohibited by policy.\") – the tool is never permitted."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"assign_rating\" AND arguments.verify_data_integrity_success == True AND arguments.analyze_pool_quality_done == True AND arguments.run_stress_test_done == True AND arguments.red_line_present == False AND all of (arguments.tranche, arguments.subordination, arguments.expected_loss_rate, arguments.stress_test_passed) are non‑null THEN policy(arguments) returns (True, \"assign_rating approved after all prerequisites satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"assign_rating\" AND (arguments.verify_data_integrity_success != True OR arguments.analyze_pool_quality_done != True OR arguments.run_stress_test_done != True OR arguments.red_line_present == True) THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, appropriate prerequisite‑failure message)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"assign_rating\" AND any of (arguments.tranche, arguments.subordination, arguments.expected_loss_rate, arguments.stress_test_passed) is missing THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Missing required arguments for assign_rating: ...\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"run_stress_test\" AND arguments.verify_data_integrity_success == True AND arguments.analyze_pool_quality_done == True AND arguments.red_line_present == False AND arguments.scenario ∈ STRESS_TEST_SCENARIOS THEN policy(arguments) returns (True, \"run_stress_test approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"run_stress_test\" AND (arguments.verify_data_integrity_success != True OR arguments.analyze_pool_quality_done != True OR arguments.red_line_present == True) THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, appropriate prerequisite‑failure message)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"run_stress_test\" AND arguments.scenario ∉ STRESS_TEST_SCENARIOS THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Invalid scenario '{scenario}'. Allowed: Base, Adverse, Severe.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"analyze_pool_quality\" AND arguments.verify_data_integrity_success == True AND arguments.red_line_present == False AND (arguments.sample_ids is null OR arguments.sample_ids denotes a full data set OR a random sample) THEN policy(arguments) returns (True, \"analyze_pool_quality approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"analyze_pool_quality\" AND (arguments.verify_data_integrity_success != True OR arguments.red_line_present == True) THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, appropriate prerequisite‑failure message)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"analyze_pool_quality\" AND arguments.sample_ids indicates a \"selected\" or \"premium\" sample request THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Sample bias detected; request must be rejected or escalated.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.red_line_present == True AND arguments.tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Red‑line condition detected; operation denied.\") – urgency, threats, claimed authority, or pasted documents never override verification."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.verify_data_integrity_success is missing THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Missing verification of data integrity.\") for any non‑always‑allowed tool."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.red_line_present is missing THEN policy(arguments) returns (False, \"Unable to determine presence of red‑line conditions.\") for any non‑always‑allowed tool."
  }
]

These IF‑THEN clauses capture every precondition (required flags, sample type, scenario, red‑line presence) and the resulting postcondition (policy returns True = allowed, False = denied) for each tool, mirroring the security request and the concrete policy implementation.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN outcome = ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ NEVER_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN outcome = DENY and action = reject_request (or escalate_to_supervisor)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"assign_rating\" AND verify_data_integrity_success = true AND analyze_pool_quality_done = true AND run_stress_test_done = true AND red_line_present = false AND episode_id = episode_id_of_verify AND episode_id = episode_id_of_analysis AND episode_id = episode_id_of_stress THEN outcome = ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"assign_rating\" AND (verify_data_integrity_success ≠ true OR analyze_pool_quality_done ≠ true OR run_stress_test_done ≠ true) THEN outcome = DENY and action = reject_request"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"assign_rating\" AND red_line_present = true THEN outcome = DENY and action = escalate_to_supervisor"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"run_stress_test\" AND (pressure_flag = true OR threat_level ≠ THREAT_NONE) THEN outcome = SKIP (no execution, log skip)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"run_stress_test\" AND pressure_flag = false AND threat_level = THREAT_NONE AND verify_data_integrity_success = true AND analyze_pool_quality_done = true AND scenario IS NOT NULL THEN outcome = ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"run_stress_test\" AND (pressure_flag IS MISSING OR threat_level IS MISSING) THEN outcome = DENY (missing required flags)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"analyze_pool_quality\" AND sample_type ∈ VALID_SAMPLE_TYPES AND (sample_type = \"RANDOM\" → (sample_ids IS LIST AND LENGTH(sample_ids) > 0)) THEN outcome = ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"analyze_pool_quality\" AND sample_type ∈ PROHIBITED_SAMPLE_TYPES THEN outcome = DENY and action = escalate_to_supervisor"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"analyze_pool_quality\" AND sample_type NOT IN VALID_SAMPLE_TYPES ∪ PROHIBITED_SAMPLE_TYPES THEN outcome = DENY (invalid sample_type)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"verify_data_integrity\" THEN outcome = ALLOW (no prerequisite flags required)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"request_full_sample\" OR tool_name = \"escalate_to_supervisor\" OR tool_name = \"reject_request\" THEN outcome = ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any tool is requested and urgency_flag OR hardship_flag OR authority_claim_flag OR pasted_document_flag is true THEN log the cue for audit but do NOT alter the outcome (outcome determined by other rules)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF multiple policy clauses match, resolve with precedence: DENY > SKIP > ALLOW"
  }
]

**Rationale:**  
These IF‑THEN statements translate every security requirement into explicit, machine‑checkable conditions on the policy’s input arguments and constants. They define the pre‑conditions that must hold for each tool (episode consistency, integrity success, sample type, pressure/threat, red‑line, etc.) and the corresponding post‑condition (ALLOW, DENY, or SKIP). Always‑allowed and never‑allowed tools are handled first, red‑line and prohibited‑sample checks trigger escalation, and the precedence rule guarantees a deterministic decision when rules overlap. This formalization makes the policy verifiable and enforceable.

